<Slide style={{ width: 1280, height: 720, background: '#0A1020', fontFamily: 'Arial', padding: '52px 60px 30px 60px', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#4D8DFF', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 2.2 }}>07 · RESULTS (5/6) — H2′</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 36, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.2, marginTop: 8 }}>
        Change the ruler and the same curve halves: 0.650 against 0.167
    </Text>
    <Box style={{ width: 1160, height: 1, background: '#24334C', marginTop: 14 }} />

    <Box style={{ marginTop: 14, padding: '12px 18px', background: '#16233A', borderLeft: '2px solid #FFB020' }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 17, color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.45 }}>
            <span style={{ color: '#FFB020', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 1 }}>H2′ — </span>
            a tenfold increase in data cannot halve the <span style={{ fontWeight: 'bold' }}>absolute</span> gain ΔR², where ΔR² = R²_chain − R²_unit.
            H2&apos;s own criterion, read on R² instead of on the ratio.
            <span style={{ color: '#A8B8CE' }}> Not pre-registered: stated after the numbers, reported beside H2, never merged into its verdict.</span>
        </Text>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', gap: 36, marginTop: 14 }}>
        <Box style={{ width: 610, flexDirection: 'column' }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 13, color: '#93A8C2', letterSpacing: 1.2, fontWeight: 'bold' }}>
                SAME FOLDS, SAME LEVELS, TWO RULERS — NORMALISED TO THE SMALLEST n
            </Text>
            <Chart
                style={{ width: 610, height: 268, marginTop: 6 }}
                chartType='lineChart'
                grouping='clustered'
                colors={['#4D8DFF', '#FFB020']}
                background='#0E1728'
                showLegend={true}
                showDataLabels={false}
                legendColor='#A8B8CE'
                axisColor='#A8B8CE'
                dataLabelColor='#FFFFFF'
                data={[
                    ['training rows', 'Λ (ratio)', 'ΔR² (absolute)'],
                    ['300', 1.0, 1.0],
                    ['1,000', 1.707, 0.948],
                    ['3,000', 1.247, 0.453],
                    ['10,000', 0.945, 0.276],
                    ['all', 0.65, 0.167],
                ]}
            />
        </Box>

        <Box style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'column', gap: 10 }}>
            <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', gap: 34 }}>
                <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'column' }}>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 36, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#4D8DFF', lineHeight: 1.05 }}>0.650</Text>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#A8B8CE', marginTop: 4, lineHeight: 1.35 }}>Λ ratio [0.570, 0.739]<br />not halved</Text>
                </Box>
                <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'column' }}>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 36, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFB020', lineHeight: 1.05 }}>0.167</Text>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#A8B8CE', marginTop: 4, lineHeight: 1.35 }}>ΔR² ratio [0.138, 0.198]<br />halved</Text>
                </Box>
            </Box>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 18, color: '#C3D0E2', lineHeight: 1.45 }}>
                The two intervals <span style={{ color: '#FFFFFF', fontWeight: 'bold' }}>do not overlap</span> — not a marginal disagreement between two metrics.
            </Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 16, color: '#A8B8CE', lineHeight: 1.45 }}>
                Mechanism: at 1,000 rows the denominator 1 − R²_unit has already halved (0.135 → 0.075) while ΔR² barely moved
                (×0.95) — that is the hump. End to end ΔR² falls ×6 and the denominator ×4, so the ratio only falls to ×0.65.
                Arithmetic, not physics.
            </Text>
        </Box>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ marginTop: 'auto', padding: '12px 18px', background: '#111B2E', borderLeft: '2px solid #4D8DFF' }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 16, color: '#C3D0E2', lineHeight: 1.45 }}>
            Two rulers, two questions: Λ asks how much of the <span style={{ fontStyle: 'italic' }}>remaining</span> variance is recovered; ΔR² asks how far R² rises in absolute terms.
            At 22,242 rows ΔR² is 0.0066 — the same order as the per-task floor (median 0.0046, maximum 0.0195).
        </Text>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between', marginTop: 10 }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8FA3BC' }}>The homopolymer is not halved under either ruler — Λ rises 11.6× [1.4, 83] from the smallest n to all.</Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8FA3BC' }}>12 / 18</Text>
    </Box>
</Slide>
